 "94bbae5a-5c35-5193-8952-f4496b15cf35" 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670744 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 5 y \\tan{(6 x )}=- 12 \\sin{(6 x )}" 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670744 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670744 1083 #uuid "97ce91ec-57ab-58d6-a70d-3b5dd8cad439" 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670745 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670731 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670745 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670745 1071 "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{- 7 x - 3 y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nAssume $x\\ne 0$." 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670745 1072 #uuid "a9aa3ffa-4834-541b-babc-7d728ab4346e" 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670745 1074 "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{- 7 x - 3 y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x^{2}\\left(\\frac{- 7 x - 3 y}{x}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x (- 7 x - 3 y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 7 x^{2} - 3 x y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(3 x)}_{P(x)}y=\\underbrace{- 7 x^{2}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 3 x y=- 7 x^{2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=3 x$ and $Q(x)=- 7 x^{2}.$" 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670746 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 2 y \\tan{(6 x )}=- 16 \\sin{(6 x )}" 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670746 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [17592186670746 1083 #uuid "ab19ae44-9d58-55e7-b811-2122760db6cd" 13194139538554 17592186045443 true] [1759